    ('b33b1575-195d-4c86-b927-cd5804b41528'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Where two main streets of Pompeii cross, the Stabian Baths rose circa 125 BC, paid for with fines. Beneath their palaestra courtyard, excavations found two previously unknown saunas.', 'The oldest and largest of Pompeii''s five public baths, built in 125 BC. A sundial with an Oscan inscription names the magistrate who ordered its construction.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b33b1575-195d-4c86-b927-cd5804b41528:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description "The oldest and largest of Pompeii''s five public baths, built in 125 BC. A sundial with an Oscan inscription names the magistrate who ordered its construction." restored on Stabian Baths, Pompeii', '8b3010921c1817b857ed1b2c31c7a72a560bf1359f77388465924d76859f4e7a|535f852ef1f7d2adbfa96caf632979fa69e23896b848a62aac915f75a837fa74|535f852ef1f7d2adbfa96caf632979fa69e23896b848a62aac915f75a837fa74', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Where two main streets of Pompeii cross, the Stabian Baths rose circa 125 BC, paid for with fines. Beneath their palaestra courtyard, excavations found two previously unknown saunas."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Stabian Baths are in Pompeii [S1]; they stand where two main streets of Pompeii cross [S2]; they were built circa 125 BC [S3, S6]; the construction was paid for with fines [S6]; they have a palaestra courtyard [S5, S7]; excavations found two previously unknown saunas beneath the palaestra courtyard [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-063 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Stabian Baths are a Roman bathing complex in Pompeii [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stabian_Baths]; They stand where two main streets of Pompeii cross [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stabian_Baths]; They were built circa 125 BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stabian_Baths]; They were paid for with fines [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stabian_Baths]; Excavations found two saunas that were previously unknown [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stabian_Baths]; The saunas lie beneath the palaestra courtyard [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stabian_Baths]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b3e5ca07-1dca-4e45-9ac8-6957093157ae'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On Kaleto Hill in Montana, the Roman fortress of Castra ad Montanesium rose in the first century AD, only to be razed to its foundations by Slav and Avar raids between 500 and 560.', 'A Roman fortress on Kaleto Hill still being investigated. Near the entrance, the ruins of a basilica mark where faith and military power once converged.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b3e5ca07-1dca-4e45-9ac8-6957093157ae:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''A Roman fortress on Kaleto Hill still being investigated. Near the entrance, the ruins of a basilica mark where faith and military power once converged.'' restored on Castra ad Montanesium', 'a56b5b581dff8a5146d57c63f4592437bce960a58e34468b77e9d31f364ad8a6|79e1e8982fab1207e3cbf104b7afdfe88d9169811a340c08cc801211defeee6e|79e1e8982fab1207e3cbf104b7afdfe88d9169811a340c08cc801211defeee6e', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On Kaleto Hill in Montana, the Roman fortress of Castra ad Montanesium rose in the first century AD, only to be razed to its foundations by Slav and Avar raids between 500 and 560."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is on Kaleto Hill [S3]; it is in Montana [S1, S3]; Castra ad Montanesium is a Roman fortress [S1]; the fortress was built in the first century AD [S4]; it was destroyed down to its foundations [S6]; the destruction was caused by Slav and Avar raids [S6]; the raids took place between 500 and 560 [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-064 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Castra ad Montanesium is a fortress (a fort) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; The fortress is Roman [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; It is in the town of Montana, Bulgaria [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; It stands on Kaleto Hill [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; It was built in the first century AD [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; It was destroyed by raids of the Slavs and Avars [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; The raids took place between 500 and 560 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]; The fortress was destroyed down to its foundations [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castra_ad_Montanesium]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b4666064-903d-4db2-a282-38897ac4c1a1'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On a rocky knoll by Loch Dunvegan, Dun Fiadhairt Broch gave up 59 amber beads, presumably a necklace, and a clay object thought to be a Roman votive model of a bale of wool.', 'Dun Fiadhairt is an Iron Age broch located on the north coast of the island of Skye. Dun Fiadhairt was excavated around 1892 by the Countess Vincent Baillet de Latour.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b4666064-903d-4db2-a282-38897ac4c1a1:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''Dun Fiadhairt is an Iron Age broch located on the north coast of the island of Skye. Dun Fiadhairt was excavated around 1892 by the Countess Vincent Baillet de Latour.'' restored on Dun Fiadhairt Broch', '1770aeff03518839dea7406fbd085d9cf3902a1ff39670be2ac095b4592bb862|ebee0117aa2b1fc17d3306f41e6ffdbd7a0acd90f156b8ff784ebc051b487176|ebee0117aa2b1fc17d3306f41e6ffdbd7a0acd90f156b8ff784ebc051b487176', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On a rocky knoll by Loch Dunvegan, Dun Fiadhairt Broch gave up 59 amber beads, presumably a necklace, and a clay object thought to be a Roman votive model of a bale of wool."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the broch stands on a rocky knoll [S2]; it is by Loch Dunvegan [S2]; 59 amber beads were found at the broch [S7]; the amber beads presumably formed a necklace [S7]; a clay object was found there [S8]; the clay object is thought to be a Roman votive model of a bale of wool [S8]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-064 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Dun Fiadhairt is a broch [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; The broch stands on a rocky knoll [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; It is by Loch Dunvegan [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; 59 amber beads were found [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; The beads presumably formed a necklace [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; A clay object was found [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; The clay object is thought to be a Roman votive model [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]; The votive model represents a bale of wool [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dun_Fiadhairt]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b4d3bc67-e38d-4d6e-9b03-0ca72a0d4398'::uuid, 'card_description', 'High in Cann Woods, Boringdon Camp looks down the Plym Valley to Plymouth Sound. An 8-metre rampart rings this Iron Age and Roman earthwork, though trees now hide part of its defences.', 'An Iron Age and Roman earthwork on a hilltop in woodland. The site has been closed to visitors since 2016 due to erosion from foot traffic.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b4d3bc67-e38d-4d6e-9b03-0ca72a0d4398:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''An Iron Age and Roman earthwork on a hilltop in woodland. The site has been closed to visitors since 2016 due to erosion from foot traffic.'' restored on Boringdon Camp', '99d1f804dee6e405d6532e4bdb1858d186113d794e6f34af72461fba9548d67e|be73f202c9b284ebe3f4c6c32a634430cab27db328ab6d016ee53cecf1792c59|be73f202c9b284ebe3f4c6c32a634430cab27db328ab6d016ee53cecf1792c59', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "High in Cann Woods, Boringdon Camp looks down the Plym Valley to Plymouth Sound. An 8-metre rampart rings this Iron Age and Roman earthwork, though trees now hide part of its defences."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Boringdon Camp is in Cann Woods [S1]; it stands high up, on a hilltop [S2]; it looks down the Plym Valley to Plymouth Sound [S2]; an 8-metre rampart surrounds it [S4]; it is an Iron Age and Roman earthwork [S1]; trees now cover part of its defences [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-064 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Boringdon Camp is an earthwork (a fort) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]; It lies in Cann Woods [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]; It is Iron Age and Roman [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]; It stands high, on a hilltop [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]; It looks down the Plym Valley to Plymouth Sound [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]; An 8-metre rampart rings the enclosure [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]; Trees now cover part of its defences [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boringdon_Camp]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b50b9e02-1fb6-42e5-9850-f463acd49604'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Beneath a 25 meter high cliff on the Río Mula, Neanderthals once lived in Cueva Antón, where a shell at least 43,000 years old was found, still bearing orange pigment.', 'A cave inhabited by Neanderthals in the Middle Paleolithic. A painted scallop shell found in 2010 proved Neanderthals used symbolic objects — a cognitive breakthrough.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b50b9e02-1fb6-42e5-9850-f463acd49604:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''A cave inhabited by Neanderthals in the Middle Paleolithic. A painted scallop shell found in 2010 proved Neanderthals used symbolic objects — a cognitive breakthrough.'' restored on Cueva Antón', '8a252091f84f0e0ad0028a7cf9c18ec4670485c3843bad4956750cc7d36cbbdd|26a1e3048cb309d3d83515904de6d187657ace325c6ebe8ba7d8ad7a767f8fcb|26a1e3048cb309d3d83515904de6d187657ace325c6ebe8ba7d8ad7a767f8fcb', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Beneath a 25 meter high cliff on the Río Mula, Neanderthals once lived in Cueva Antón, where a shell at least 43,000 years old was found, still bearing orange pigment."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cueva Anton lies at the base of a 25 meter high cliff [S7]; the cliff is on the Rio Mula [S7]; Neanderthals once lived in the cave [S3]; a shell at least 43,000 years old was found there [S4]; the shell bore orange pigment [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-064 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cueva Antón is a cave [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]; Neanderthals lived in the cave [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]; The cave lies beneath a 25 meter high cliff [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]; The cliff is on the Río Mula [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]; A shell was found there [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]; The shell is at least 43,000 years old [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]; The shell bears orange pigment [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cueva_Ant%C3%B3n]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b69f338c-fb2b-4860-9935-61e93e27ddf3'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Two slender stones, each about 3 m high yet only about 20 cm thick, stand on Holy Island: the Penrhos Feilw Standing Stones, thought to be Bronze Age, their origins and purpose unclear.', 'Two Bronze Age standing stones, each about 3 metres tall but only 20 cm thick. They stand 3 metres apart like thin blades driven into the earth.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b69f338c-fb2b-4860-9935-61e93e27ddf3:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''Two Bronze Age standing stones, each about 3 metres tall but only 20 cm thick. They stand 3 metres apart like thin blades driven into the earth.'' restored on Penrhos Feilw Standing Stones', '298777cf4a906d430a1308677875bebb4ec98e2b1f3e39ec441b5386b6ce42ce|72b68dc9e9cb1f7b40d87f6344c3a72acd333c1c6024feebfbeace91d8f69760|72b68dc9e9cb1f7b40d87f6344c3a72acd333c1c6024feebfbeace91d8f69760', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Two slender stones, each about 3 m high yet only about 20 cm thick, stand on Holy Island: the Penrhos Feilw Standing Stones, thought to be Bronze Age, their origins and purpose unclear."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Penrhos Feilw Standing Stones are two stones [S1]; the stones are slender [S4]; each stone is about 3 m high [S4]; each stone is only about 20 cm thick [S4]; they stand on Holy Island [S1]; they are thought to be Bronze Age [S2]; their origins and purpose are unclear [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-064 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Penrhos Feilw is a site of stan