    ('b740c74a-83ce-4e01-a07c-87ab90574750'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On an east-facing scarp, the three stelae and altar of Tres Islas mimic the E-Group at Uaxactun, a perfect place to watch the sunrise at this Early Classic Maya capital.', 'Maya site dated to 400 BC with three stelae and an altar arranged as an E-Group astronomical complex. A monument to Maya celestial observation, active from the Late Preclassic period.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b740c74a-83ce-4e01-a07c-87ab90574750:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''Maya site dated to 400 BC with three stelae and an altar arranged as an E-Group astronomical complex. A monument to Maya celestial observation, active from the Late Preclassic period.'' restored on Tres Islas', '6a4a45f7d4d0e3341b3826306ef3d9a1c4013fd6980a13baaa5c5677759dd614|8a4721ae6636f5b6a8abb11d8b85a1b54837b51c173599a87a12c147e8e17e1f|8a4721ae6636f5b6a8abb11d8b85a1b54837b51c173599a87a12c147e8e17e1f', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On an east-facing scarp, the three stelae and altar of Tres Islas mimic the E-Group at Uaxactun, a perfect place to watch the sunrise at this Early Classic Maya capital."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the monuments stand on an east-facing scarp [S7]; Tres Islas has three stelae and an altar [S2]; the stelae and altar mimic the E-Group at Uaxactun [S6]; the spot is a perfect place to watch the sunrise [S7]; Tres Islas is a Maya site [S1]; Tres Islas was an Early Classic capital [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-065 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Tres Islas is a Maya archaeological site (an Early Classic capital) in Guatemala [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tres_Islas]; Tres Islas is in Guatemala [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tres_Islas]; The site''s main feature is three stelae and an altar [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tres_Islas]; The stelae and altar mimic the E-Group at Uaxactun [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tres_Islas]; The group stands on an east-facing scarp [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tres_Islas]; The location is perfect for watching the sunrise [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tres_Islas]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b7ce5331-6c35-46bb-ac93-fdccf2b208e0'::uuid, 'card_description', 'In the Moche Valley, Caballo Muerto holds a dozen ceremonial buildings on platforms, walls decorated with reliefs of snakes and cats, its people living off land reclaimed from the desert.', 'The archaeological complex of Caballo Muerto features stone and adobe constructions, with mud used as mortar.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:b7ce5331-6c35-46bb-ac93-fdccf2b208e0:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''The archaeological complex of Caballo Muerto features stone and adobe constructions, with mud used as mortar.'' restored on Caballo Muerto', 'dc5120e0a99e90d150bc6df051bc6e8bbeae34206fba073a3b328bc1bee1ace0|1823d163ced78f04815268dd4726f733d480d6af8ab1d4cbec6edbd23f4ddc28|1823d163ced78f04815268dd4726f733d480d6af8ab1d4cbec6edbd23f4ddc28', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In the Moche Valley, Caballo Muerto holds a dozen ceremonial buildings on platforms, walls decorated with reliefs of snakes and cats, its people living off land reclaimed from the desert."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Caballo Muerto is in the Moche Valley [S1, S2]; it holds a dozen ceremonial buildings [S5]; the buildings stand on platforms [S5]; walls are decorated with reliefs of snakes and cats [S7]; its people lived off land reclaimed from the desert [S8]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-065 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Caballo Muerto is an archaeological complex of mound sites in Peru [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; It is in the Moche Valley [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; It holds a dozen buildings [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; The buildings are ceremonial [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; The buildings stand on platforms [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; Walls are decorated with reliefs of snakes [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; Walls are decorated with reliefs of cats [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]; Its people lived off land reclaimed from the desert [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caballo_Muerto]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ba7e3421-2f30-4f00-91e4-52d989e50000'::uuid, 'card_description', 'On a high ridge in Epping Forest, a low bank and ditch still circle Loughton Camp, an Iron Age hill fort. Its banks were most probably once a single high rampart, used for defence.', 'Loughton Camp is an Iron Age Hill fort in Epping Forest, one mile northwest of the town of Loughton.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:ba7e3421-2f30-4f00-91e4-52d989e50000:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''Loughton Camp is an Iron Age Hill fort in Epping Forest, one mile northwest of the town of Loughton.'' restored on Loughton Camp', '84cb65a99c24cb5876adba48bf54b32ba1c1104bb7ca81de0d1509c34a706a0e|94e109bf5a7d3b77ab0bd5058a284abbc7eadb87e204371c17e014cd9af946c4|94e109bf5a7d3b77ab0bd5058a284abbc7eadb87e204371c17e014cd9af946c4', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "On a high ridge in Epping Forest, a low bank and ditch still circle Loughton Camp, an Iron Age hill fort. Its banks were most probably once a single high rampart, used for defence."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Loughton Camp lies on a high ridge [S4]; it is in Epping Forest [S1]; a low bank and ditch still encircle it [S2]; it is an Iron Age hill fort [S1]; its banks were most probably once a single high rampart [S3]; the rampart was used for defence [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-065 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Loughton Camp is a hill fort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughton_Camp]; It dates to the Iron Age [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loughton_Camp]; It 