    ('bb724fd3-aa84-4a86-a22f-2a6f5e267797'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Near Land''s End, a stone rampart and ditch cut across a headland with almost sheer cliffs on two sides: Maen Castle, one of only two Cornish fortified sites to yield Early Iron Age pottery.', 'An Iron Age cliff castle near Land''s End, one of only two fortified sites in its county where early Iron Age pottery has been found. A stone rampart blocks the only landward approach.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:bb724fd3-aa84-4a86-a22f-2a6f5e267797:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description "An Iron Age cliff castle near Land''s End, one of only two fortified sites in its county where early Iron Age pottery has been found. A stone rampart blocks the only landward approach." restored on Maen Castle', 'b8aec4cf898a344228e2955a4d01a6f3ced83fb732035192c8e55b579911fd82|84ea0cfb61fb5bbeafb894c4c404127a1385b000decdc27c5141a16c301b41c1|84ea0cfb61fb5bbeafb894c4c404127a1385b000decdc27c5141a16c301b41c1', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Near Land''s End, a stone rampart and ditch cut across a headland with almost sheer cliffs on two sides: Maen Castle, one of only two Cornish fortified sites to yield Early Iron Age pottery."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Maen Castle is near Land''s End [S1]; a stone rampart and ditch cut across a headland [S4]; the headland has almost sheer cliffs on two sides [S4]; Maen Castle is a fortified site in Cornwall [S1, S2]; it is one of only two Cornish fortified sites that yielded Early Iron Age pottery [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-065 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Maen Castle is an Iron Age promontory fort (a fortified site) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]; It is near Land''s End [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]; It has a stone rampart [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]; It has a ditch [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]; The defences cut across a headland [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]; The headland has almost sheer cliffs on two sides [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]; It is one of only two Cornish fortified sites to yield Early Iron Age pottery [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maen_Castle]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('bd8def7d-14df-4ba8-902f-a2ba0d93fdd6'::uuid, 'card_description', 'At the edge of a wood in Gloucestershire lies Nympsfield Long Barrow, built around 2800 BC. Within it 23 bodies were found, and cremated children rested in a cist of their own.', 'Built around 2800 BC and measuring 27 by 18 metres, Nympsfield holds multiple separate chambers. Curving walls frame the trapezoidal entrance to the mound.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:bd8def7d-14df-4ba8-902f-a2ba0d93fdd6:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''Built around 2800 BC and measuring 27 by 18 metres, Nympsfield holds multiple separate chambers. Curving walls frame the trapezoidal entrance to the mound.'' restored on Nympsfield Long Barrow', '828d9249947caeb32be3b178c74cc6c3fc930a01e285f942e67b7a14c465c998|483436d0b0ea36ae824cc3806a02dec4d687c860c4fb68ad6f4a0ec8df3bd92c|483436d0b0ea36ae824cc3806a02dec4d687c860c4fb68ad6f4a0ec8df3bd92c', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "At the edge of a wood in Gloucestershire lies Nympsfield Long Barrow, built around 2800 BC. Within it 23 bodies were found, and cremated children rested in a cist of their own."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the barrow lies at the edge of a wood [S2]; it is in Gloucestershire [S1]; it was built around 2800 BC [S4]; 23 bodies were found within it [S7]; cremated children were placed in a separate cist [S8]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-065 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Nympsfield Long Barrow is a Neolithic burial barrow in Gloucestershire [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nympsfield_Long_Barrow]; It lies at the edge of a wood [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nympsfield_Long_Barrow]; It was built around 2800 BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nympsfield_Long_Barrow]; 23 bodies were found within it [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nympsfield_Long_Barrow]; Cremated children were placed in a separate cist [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nympsfield_Long_Barrow]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('bf395f91-b77b-460f-802b-20cf52a73bfb'::uuid, 'card_description', 'In the Preseli Mountains, Waun Mawn may once have held a Neolithic stone circle which, it has been argued, was taken apart, dragged across land and reassembled at Stonehenge.', 'Waun Mawn is a megalithic site in the Preseli Mountains of Pembrokeshire. The site is located around 1 mile to the southwest of Brynberian.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:bf395f91-b77b-460f-802b-20cf52a73bfb:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''Waun Mawn is a megalithic site in the Preseli Mountains of Pembrokeshire. The site is located around 1 mile to the southwest of Brynberian.'' restored on Waun Mawn', '83be4a5ae607e1d99ccb1099f8f44f1dea5b6ddd1d1f7182ba119ca38e318a78|d1b8fe4ba8929061902151708beb5626fc4ba0ccbaaa1f58a564fd7b2fe60297|d1b8fe4ba8929061902151708beb5626fc4ba0ccbaaa1f58a564fd7b2fe60297', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In the Preseli Mountains, Waun Mawn may once have held a Neolithic stone circle which, it has been argued, was taken apart, dragged across land and reassembled at Stonehenge."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Waun Mawn is in the Preseli Mountains [S1]; it may once have held a Neolithic stone circle [S2, S4]; it has been argued that the circle was taken apart [S5]; it has been argued that the stones were dragged across land [S5]; it has been argued that the circle was reassembled at Stonehenge [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-066 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Waun Mawn is a megalithic site [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]; Waun Mawn lies in the Preseli Mountains, Wales [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]; Waun Mawn may once have held a stone circle [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]; The possible stone circle was Neolithic [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]; It has been argued the circle was taken apart [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]; It has been argued the stones were dragged across land [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]; It has been argued the stones were reassembled at Stonehenge [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waun_Mawn]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('bf3e61c6-0ecc-4223-949e-86afe1d8d2ac'::uuid, 'card_description', 'The 277-metre hill of Pilsdon Pen, at the north end of the Marshwood Vale, is crowned by an Iron Age Durotrigian hillfort. Near its centre, the remains of 14 roundhouses were uncovered.', 'A multivallate Durotrigian hillfort crowns a 277-metre hill in Dorset. Fourteen hut foundations found within suggest a sizable settled community on the summit.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:bf3e61c6-0ecc-4223-949e-86afe1d8d2ac:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''A multivallate Durotrigian hillfort crowns a 277-metre hill in Dorset. Fourteen hut foundations found within suggest a sizable settled community on the summit.'' restored on Pilsdon Pen', 'a0ca662a873df745b58ab839210b3cf543dfe4cb93fe6d5121844a3d06620862|8fd1b421e5baaa70dc42396c4d28584855573c299506c5df01a0dbef43663d13|8fd1b421e5baaa70dc42396c4d28584855573c299506c5df01a0dbef43663d13', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The 277-metre hill of Pilsdon Pen, at the north end of the Marshwood Vale, is crowned by an Iron Age Durotrigian hillfort. Near its centre, the remains of 14 roundhouses were uncovered."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Pilsdon Pen is a 277-metre hill [S1]; it is at the north end of the Marshwood Vale [S1]; the hill is topped by a hillfort [S3]; the hillfort is Iron Age and Durotrigian [S3]; the remains of 14 roundhouses were uncovered near the centre of the hillfort [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-066 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Pilsdon Pen is a hill 277 metres high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]; Pilsdon Pen lies at the north end of the Marshwood Vale [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]; The hill is crowned by a hillfort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]; The hillfort dates to the Iron Age [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]; The hillfort is Durotrigian [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]; The remains of 14 roundhouses were uncovered [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]; The roundhouses were near the centre of the hillfort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilsdon_Pen]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c0319301-7c5f-42bc-9af0-808880e776c2'::uuid, 'card_description', 'In the woods of the South Harz, rampart and ditch mark the Grasburg, a prehistoric refuge castle and by legend the seat of the counts of Stolberg, where a 13th century chapel drew pilgrims.', 'A prehistoric refuge hillfort in the Harz mountains with rampart-and-ditch defenses. Legend claims it as the ancestral seat of the counts of Stolberg.', 'teaser-card-s025-rollback:c0319301-7c5f-42bc-9af0-808880e776c2:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s025: card_description ''A prehistoric refuge hillfort in the Harz mountains with rampart-and-ditch defenses. Legend claims it as the ancestral seat of the counts of Stolberg.'' restored on Grasburg, Rottleberode', '1a313192da6242b7708706f87d21c8c85ef95102c82934b60048ce96f749ab02|c29d18adbc738dcdd53d07aa12d50264a9f0c885c53856b8aec663c755668b44|c29d18adbc738dcdd53d07aa12d50264a9f0c885c53856b8aec663c755668b44', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-write-022", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In the woods of the South Harz, rampart and ditch mark the Grasburg, a prehistoric refuge castle and by legend the seat of the counts of Stolberg, where a 13th century chapel drew pilgrims."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-check-022 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Grasburg lies in a wooded area [S2]; it is in the South Harz [S2]; it has a rampart and ditch [S1]; the Grasburg is a prehistoric refuge castle [S1]; by legend it was the seat of the counts of Stolberg [S2]; a chapel was built there in the 13th century [S3]; the chapel was a pilgrimage chapel that drew pilgrims [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-05: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-05-verify-066 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-05/